.nh
.TH "PB-PORT-NAME-LIST" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-port-name-list - List the workspace's port names


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb port name list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
List the port names of the active workspace: names of its machines' ports, its
all-machines names and its top-level names. A top-level name whose label is also a
machine's name is shown as shadowed: that address opens the machine.

.PP
JSON output is supported with --json.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print JSON


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-port-name(1)\fP
